@page "/"
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IShellSettings Settings
@inject StudioShellDescriptor Descriptor

@*
    The shell's front page, at the mount itself (v2 step 5). It is a page of no module, so the layout draws no scope selector and no gate around it.

    With one module composed there is nothing to choose, and no page is drawn: the visitor is sent to the module's home, with the query string they
    came with (a scope in a pasted link survives). A request for the address is answered by its endpoint (StudioEndpointMapper) with a redirect that is
    a path, {PathBase}{mount}/{home}, never an absolute URL built from the request's scheme and host, which a proxy the application does not trust the
    headers of would get wrong. This component's own redirect is the circuit's: a client-side navigation to the front address, where the browser's own
    address is the base. The front address never draws a page the visitor has to click through.

    With two or more, one tile per module, in module order: the module's name, one sentence and a link to its home. A tile carries no number: a count
    of documents or topics is a gated read of the module's own, and the front page reads nothing.
*@

@if (Descriptor.Modules.Count > 1)
{
    <PageTitle>@Settings.Title</PageTitle>

    <div class="ms-page ms-front">
        <div class="ms-page-header">
            <h1 class="ms-page-title">@Settings.Title</h1>
        </div>

        <ul class="ms-front-tiles" aria-label="Modules">
            @foreach (IStudioModule module in Descriptor.Modules)
            {
                <li class="ms-front-tile-item" @key="module.Key">
                    <a class="ms-front-tile" href="@StudioLink.To(module.HomeRoute)">
                        <span class="ms-front-tile-name">@module.ProductName</span>
                        <span class="ms-front-tile-summary">@module.Summary</span>
                    </a>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    </div>
}

@code
{
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (Descriptor.Modules.Count != 1)
        {
            return;
        }

        // The mount's own path, as the browser spelled it, plus the module's home and the query the visitor came with.
        Uri current = new(Navigation.Uri);
        string target = current.AbsolutePath.TrimEnd('/') + "/" + Descriptor.Modules[0].HomeRoute + current.Query;

        Navigation.NavigateTo(target, replace: true);
    }
}
